━━━ stdout
Validate objects and queries

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide validate␛[0m [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

␛[1m␛[4mCommands:␛[0m
  ␛[1mquery␛[0m  Check rule queries offline, or on the tenants (--live)

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--check␛[0m <CHECK>
          Run one check only: id-uniqueness, uuid-format, schema, cve, sharing-config, configuration, queries
          
          [possible values: id-uniqueness, uuid-format, schema, cve, sharing-config, configuration, queries]

      ␛[1m--file␛[0m <FILE>
          Validate only this file (repeatable)

      ␛[1m--uuid␛[0m <UUID>
          Validate only the object with this UUID (repeatable)

      ␛[1m--type␛[0m <OBJECT_TYPE>
          Validate only this type: rule, threat or objective (repeatable)
          
          [possible values: rule, threat, objective]

      ␛[1m--strict␛[0m
          Fail on warnings too

      ␛[1m--queries␛[0m <error|warn|off>
          How a query the platform would reject is reported: error (the default), warn (passes unless --strict) or off (queries are not checked)
          
          [possible values: error, warn, off]

      ␛[1m--allow-empty␛[0m
          With --strict: pass a full run that finds no detection objects (the commit hook setup writes passes it)

      ␛[1m--fix␛[0m
          Apply every safe fix (vocabulary typos), then validate again

      ␛[1m--dry-run␛[0m
          With --fix: print the edits as a diff and change nothing

      ␛[1m--watch␛[0m
          Validate again each time an object file changes; Ctrl-C stops

      ␛[1m--format␛[0m <REPORT_FORMAT>
          text: code frames. sarif: SARIF 2.1.0 for code scanning. codequality: GitLab Code Quality (Code Climate JSON). A report goes to --output, or to stdout instead of the text
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, sarif, codequality]

      ␛[1m--output␛[0m <OUTPUT>
          Write the --format report to this file and print the usual text output too

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide validate
  $ opentide validate --strict --type rule
  $ opentide validate --queries warn

